From 7c5b978a33602732aaf5752d74cb844a39d4f860 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 13:32:30 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] feat(kanban): unclaimed notices start a turn, not just a
 transcript row; log poller misses [daveey]

When no live poller claimed a card's events within the grace window, the
unloaded-chat sweeper wrote a kanban_notice row and stopped. A row is not a
turn: on 2026-10-27, 19 chats sat green on such rows until David opened
them, 5 of them held by a backend whose poller never claimed the event.

The sweeper now runs ONE turn with the notice through
server._wake_session_turn on a context-bound worker thread (at most 2 at once,
one per chat), and writes the passive row only when the wake can't start, the
card is blocked on a validated human request, the notice is diagnostic-only,
the chat's per-process budget (HERMES_KANBAN_UNLOADED_WAKES_PER_HOUR, default
4, spent only by started turns) is used up, no slot is free, or
HERMES_KANBAN_UNLOADED_WAKE=0. Claimed events always end as a turn or a row:
any error after the claim falls back to the row, a failed row rewinds.

A chat another live backend holds reaching the sweeper means its poller
missed: logged at WARNING as "kanban poller miss" with the holder's pid.

test_kanban_unloaded_sweep.py specifies the passive-row path and now pins
HERMES_KANBAN_UNLOADED_WAKE=0 (autouse) instead of passing through a real
session.resume; the wake path is covered by test_kanban_unloaded_wake.py.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
